      <layout margin="40pt">
        <text font-size="l" font="Helvetica-Bold" color="primary" paginate="keep-next">One: the harbour</text>
        <text>The harbour was dug by hand in the year of the famine, and the stones of its quay came from the old church, which the storm had taken the roof off.</text>
        <text>The boats were small, and the fish were many, and the town grew around the quay as a town grows around a well.</text>
        <text font-size="l" font="Helvetica-Bold" color="primary" paginate="break-before">Two: the light</text>
        <text>The first light was a fire on the headland, kept by whoever had the wood. The second was a lamp in a tower, kept by the keepers of the record.</text>
        <text font-size="l" font="Helvetica-Bold" color="primary" paginate="break-before">Three: the museum</text>
        <text>The museum keeps the record, the old lamp and the brass bell, and lights the lamp once a year, on the night of the gale.</text>
      </layout>
    </section>

